# Logging and database conventions

## Logging

- Always add clear prefixes to `console.log`, `console.error`, `console.warn`, and `console.info` so logs are easy to identify.
- Use `[SERVER]` for server-side logs (API routes, Server Actions, server components).
- Use `[CLIENT]` for client-side logs (React components, hooks, browser code).
- Include function or component name in the prefix (e.g. `[SERVER] getLatestApprovalRequestByEventId:`, `[CLIENT] OutlookStyleCalendar:`).
- Server logs appear in the terminal where the dev server runs; browser logs appear in DevTools.

## Database operations

- NEVER create scripts (`.ts`, `.js`, `.sh`, etc.) to perform database operations, schema changes, or attribute creation.
- ALWAYS use MCP tools for all database operations.
- When attributes need to be created or modified, use the available MCP database tools (string, boolean, integer, datetime, etc.).
- If MCP tools are unavailable or fail, provide clear instructions for manual creation via Appwrite Console UI.
- Covers creating/modifying attributes, indexes, and migrations.

## Server restart indication

- After code changes, indicate whether a server restart is required:
  - Frontend-only → no restart / page refresh is enough
  - Server-side / API / env → server restart required
